drm: h713-afbd: republish the VidDec record for a memory framebuffer too

With a 1280x720 source on the HDMI ring and the keystone warp on, the wall
shows the warped picture one and a half times side by side, sheared, while
the frame h713-warp renders is correct (ctl dump, 1920x1080 NV12) and the
same source without the warp is correct as well. With a 1920x1080 source
the warp is correct. Found 05.10.2026 on the HY310, Fire TV stick at 720p60.

The reader behind the video plane is the firmware's window chain, and that
chain lays itself out from the VidDec descriptor and from nothing else
(0117 found this for the ring: the window layer, not the capture, reads
the record). h713_afbd_publish_video_info() republishes the record on a
geometry change in ring mode only; outside ring mode it refused with
"refusing to rewrite the VidDec descriptor for 1920x1080; the capture does
not survive a second signal event". So when h713-tv takes the ring down
and puts the warp's 1920x1080 NV12 framebuffer on the plane, source 0 is
programmed for the frame -- but the firmware keeps the 720p ring's layout
and reads 1920-byte lines with an 80-block (1280-byte) pitch, 720 of them,
and scales that up.

Measured through /dev/mem on the HY310, kernel 6.18.38, in three states
(bench of 05.10.2026, register snapshots kept outside the tree):

  720p, warp off (B)        720p, warp on (C, C2)       meaning
  AFBD +0x040 = 0x500       AFBD +0x040 = 0x780         luma stride: ours, follows the fb
  AFBD +0x048 = 0x02d00500  AFBD +0x048 = 0x04380780    crop: ours, follows the fb
  AFBD +0x070 = 0x4c3ef000  AFBD +0x070 = 0x77d00000    ring slot -> the warp's dumb buffer
  AFBD +0x030 = 0x02d00500  AFBD +0x030 = 0x02d00500    firmware's word: 720x1280, unchanged
  0x05000444 = 0x02d00500   0x05000444 = 0x02d00500     composition geometry: 720x1280
  0x05000434 = 0x80500050   0x05000434 = 0x80500050     composition pitch: 80 blocks = 1280
  0x05180034 = 0x050002d0   0x05180034 = 0x050002d0     picture scaler input: 1280x720
  descriptor words 2..5,22  = 1280 720 1280 720 .. 1280 in both states
  INCAP +0x924 = 0x00500050 in both (the ring itself is untouched)

dmesg at every claim: "refusing to rewrite the VidDec descriptor for
1920x1080". With a 1080p source the two records are identical, nothing is
refused and nothing is wrong, which is why the warp passed every test at
1080p60 since 22.09. The projector's own camera over "ctl test grid" shows
two interleaved families of grid lines (the bench's camera shot); the
GPU's frame (the bench's GPU dump) shows one clean grid.

So the record is republished for a memory framebuffer as it is for the
ring: with the frame's geometry and stride, and without a window -- a
memory frame is the plane's own picture, the KMS source rectangle is the
whole framebuffer (atomic_check) and the firmware is told the same. That
also closes a second hole measured today: a "zoom in 2" set on the ring
before the warp claims leaves src-window in the plane state (h713-tv does
not clear it), the ring record carried it, and the firmware zoomed into
the centre of the warped frame (scaler window 640x360, regs-Z2). The
marker/wait for the WCE now runs for every new publication and not only
for NV16, so the enable waits until the firmware has rebuilt its chain for
the record it was just handed, and says so if it has not.

Cost: the publication switches the capture off and the capture owner
re-arms it (0099), as for every ring geometry change today -- now also at
each warp claim and release on a source that is not the panel's size. The
ring the warp reads through V4L2 is laid out by INCAP, which the record
does not reach (0117, and INCAP +0x924 above); the warp's stream sees the
same ~170 ms gap a ring geometry change costs.

Not built and not run on the device yet: the bench had no kernel build and
no flashing in scope. What to verify after it is: with a 720p source and
the warp on, 0x05000444 must read 0x04380780, 0x05000434 0x80780078,
0x05180034 0x07800438, the descriptor words 2..5 1920 1080 1920 1080 and
INCAP +0x924 still 0x00500050; the camera over "ctl test grid" one grid.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
@@ -577,6 +577,30 @@
  * with a source switch. That is the same mechanism a first publication already
  * relies on, now used a second time.
  *
+ * And the same holds WITHOUT the ring. A framebuffer fetched from memory (the
+ * keystone warp's NV12 frames, h713-warp since 23.09.2026) is read by the very
+ * same window chain, and that chain takes its geometry and its line pitch from
+ * this record and from nothing else. Until 05.10.2026 the record was refused a
+ * rewrite outside ring mode, so with a 1280x720 source on the ring the warp's
+ * 1920x1080 frame was read as 720 lines of 1280 bytes and scaled up from there:
+ * the wall showed the picture one and a half times side by side, sheared.
+ * Measured on the HY310 through /dev/mem with the plane programmed for the
+ * warp's frame (AFBD +0x040 = 0x780, +0x048 = 0x04380780, the buffer at
+ * 0x77d00000): the firmware's own words still said 1280x720 and 80 blocks a
+ * line -- AFBD +0x030 = 0x02d00500, the composition block's 0x05000444 =
+ * 0x02d00500 and 0x05000434 = 0x80500050, the picture scaler's 0x05180034 =
+ * 0x050002d0 -- and the descriptor page itself still read 1280 720 ... 1280,
+ * while dmesg carried the refusal for 1920x1080. With a 1920x1080 source the
+ * two records were identical, nothing was refused and the warp was right,
+ * which is why this took two weeks to show. The record is republished for a
+ * memory framebuffer now, with the frame's own geometry and stride and, since
+ * a memory frame is the plane's own picture and not a ring the firmware fills,
+ * without a window: the KMS source rectangle is the whole framebuffer there
+ * (atomic_check) and the firmware is told the same. A window left standing in
+ * the plane state from a zoom on the ring (h713-tv does not clear it before
+ * the warp's commit) would otherwise zoom the warped picture a second time --
+ * measured, the scaler window went to 640x360 over the warp's frame.
+ *
  * Returns true if the firmware has something new to look at here, i.e. if the
  * record or the pointer changed. See h713_afbd_wait_wce().
  */
@@ -597,13 +621,16 @@
 				   ring ? h->mode.hdisplay : w,
 				   ring ? h->mode.vdisplay : hgt,
 				   h->mode.hdisplay, h->mode.vdisplay,
-				   src_win, dst_win, aspect);
+				   ring ? src_win : NULL, ring ? dst_win : NULL,
+				   aspect);
 	differs = memcmp(h->video_info, rec, sizeof(rec)) != 0;
-	write_record = differs && (!h->video_info_published || ring);
-	if (differs && h->video_info_published && !ring)
-		drm_warn(&h->drm,
-			 "refusing to rewrite the VidDec descriptor for %ux%u; the capture does not survive a second signal event\n",
-			 w, hgt);
+	write_record = differs;
+	if (differs && h->video_info_published)
+		drm_info(&h->drm,
+			 "republishing the VidDec descriptor for the %s %ux%u, stride %u (was %ux%u, stride %u): the firmware's window chain follows the record\n",
+			 ring ? "ring" : "framebuffer", w, hgt, stride,
+			 ((const u32 *)h->video_info)[2], ((const u32 *)h->video_info)[3],
+			 ((const u32 *)h->video_info)[22]);
 
 	if (write_record) {
 		memcpy(h->video_info, rec, sizeof(rec));
@@ -948,10 +974,10 @@
 		/*
 		 * The VideoInfo pointers stay. Clearing them takes the frame
 		 * descriptor away from the firmware, which then has to be
-		 * re-published to enable the plane again -- and a second
-		 * publish is the one thing this hardware does not survive
-		 * (see h713_afbd_publish_video_info()). The pointer costs
-		 * nothing while source 0 is off.
+		 * re-published to enable the plane again; a publication
+		 * switches the capture off and costs the capture owner a
+		 * re-arm (see h713_afbd_publish_video_info()), and the
+		 * pointer costs nothing while source 0 is off.
 		 */
 	}
 	writel(0, h->regs + AFBD_VIDEO_AUX_Y);
@@ -1004,8 +1030,13 @@
  * lines has ever reached the ring (E3).
  *
  * Without the ring the buffer is fetched from memory, and there the old rule
- * stands: the buffer has to be the panel size, because nothing behind the
- * reader gets reprogrammed for it.
+ * stands: the buffer has to be the panel size. What is behind the reader IS
+ * reprogrammed for it -- the firmware lays its window chain out from the
+ * descriptor, which h713_afbd_publish_video_info() republishes with the
+ * framebuffer's geometry whenever it differs from the record that stands --
+ * but a frame that is not the panel's size would then be scaled by that
+ * chain, and that scaler is the firmware's and has been measured for the
+ * ring only. The one memory client there is renders the panel's size.
  */
 static bool h713_afbd_window_ok(const struct drm_property_blob *b,
 				const struct drm_display_mode *m)
@@ -1205,13 +1236,19 @@
 		h713_afbd_wait_ready(h, AFBD_READY, "RGB disable");
 
 		/*
-		 * Park the marker before the firmware can see the descriptor,
-		 * and only for NV16. For NV12 the chroma stride the WCE
-		 * computes from the record is the one this plane wants anyway,
-		 * so there is nothing to lose there and nothing to wait for.
+		 * Park the marker before the firmware can see the descriptor.
+		 * For NV16 the wait below protects the doubled chroma stride.
+		 * For NV12 the chroma stride the WCE computes from the record
+		 * is the one this plane wants anyway, but the wait is still
+		 * what tells us the firmware has rebuilt its chain for a NEW
+		 * record -- a memory framebuffer that follows a ring of
+		 * another geometry (the warp over a 720p source) is such a
+		 * record since 05.10.2026, and an enable that programs source
+		 * 0 before the chain follows shows the old layout for as long
+		 * as the firmware takes. The marker is written for real a few
+		 * lines below in every case, so it never reaches the panel.
 		 */
-		if (nv16)
-			writel(0, h->regs + AFBD_VIDEO_C_STRIDE);
+		writel(0, h->regs + AFBD_VIDEO_C_STRIDE);
 		/*
 		 * The record keeps the RING's geometry, not the crop: the
 		 * firmware rebuilds its capture chain from it
@@ -1226,10 +1263,12 @@
 							 h713_afbd_window(s->src_window),
 							 h713_afbd_window(s->dst_window),
 							 s->aspect);
-		if (published && nv16 && h713_afbd_wait_wce(h))
+		if (published && h713_afbd_wait_wce(h))
 			drm_err(&h->drm,
-				"firmware did not reprogram the chroma stride within %u ms of the descriptor; source 0 is programmed anyway, so this enable may come up with a halved chroma stride\n",
-				H713_WCE_TIMEOUT_US / 1000);
+				"firmware did not reprogram the chroma stride within %u ms of the descriptor; source 0 is programmed anyway, so this enable may come up with %s\n",
+				H713_WCE_TIMEOUT_US / 1000,
+				nv16 ? "a halved chroma stride" :
+				       "the window chain still laid out for the previous record");
 	}
 
 	writel(h713_video_size_m1(w, hgt), h->regs + AFBD_VIDEO_SIZE_M1);
